WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.423
A control is a process, activity, configuration, review,

00:00:03.423 --> 00:00:07.576
or safeguard that helps an organization meet a trust objective.

00:00:07.576 --> 00:00:12.560
Controls may be technical, administrative, operational, or a combination of several types.

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.883
Examples include access reviews, change approvals, vulnerability management,

00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:19.621
incident response procedures, security awareness training, monitoring, backup testing,

00:00:19.621 --> 00:00:22.528
vendor review, risk assessment, and policy acknowledgment.

00:00:22.528 --> 00:00:27.928
Evidence is the record that shows a control exists and operates as intended.

00:00:27.928 --> 00:00:33.327
Auditors evaluate evidence to understand whether the organization followed the process it described.

00:00:33.327 --> 00:00:37.481
Evidence may include policies, procedures, tickets, approvals, screenshots, logs, reports,

00:00:37.481 --> 00:00:41.219
training records, meeting notes, system configurations, access review results,

00:00:41.219 --> 00:00:43.296
monitoring alerts, or incident records.

00:00:43.296 --> 00:00:46.203
Good evidence usually comes from normal work.

00:00:46.203 --> 00:00:51.187
If a team already uses tickets, code reviews, approval workflows, identity systems,

00:00:51.187 --> 00:00:56.171
monitoring platforms, and training tools consistently, those records can become audit evidence.

00:00:56.171 --> 00:00:58.248
Poor evidence practices create friction.

00:00:58.248 --> 00:01:04.063
If work happens informally, if approvals are not recorded, if tickets are missing context,

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:09.462
or if ownership is unclear, teams may struggle to show what happened later.

00:01:09.462 --> 00:01:14.862
For employees, the lesson is simple: follow the process and document the work.

00:01:14.862 --> 00:01:18.184
Clear records help the organization demonstrate accountability, consistency,

00:01:18.184 --> 00:01:19.430
and operational discipline.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:25.661
Evidence quality improves when teams capture the right information at the time the work happens.

00:01:25.661 --> 00:01:31.060
Waiting until later often leads to missing context, unclear approvals, or unnecessary rework.
